  "Question": "Subtraction with borrowing requires borrowing 1 from the tens place and treating it as 10. In \\(32-7\\), there are not enough ones to subtract. What should you do?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Borrow 1 from the tens place and treat it as 10",
    "B": "Carry 1 to the ones place",
    "C": "Simply subtract 2 from 7"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "After borrowing 1, the ones calculation is \\(12-7=5\\), and 2 remains in the tens place, giving 25.",
